what is aws egress-only internet gateways 

egress-only internet gateways is used for ipv6 internet access in your private subnet 
this mean you have private subnet where you hosted your aws instances that you want it to access
internet. if your instances are ipv4 you can use Nat gateways but if you use ipv6 you can use 
egress-only internet gateways which is stateful mean it will allow returned request and you 
can only ask the request mean it allows outbound internet traffic only not inbound traffic


aws transitive routing allow your vpc A to communicate vpc C through vpc B
it allows to communicate to network that does not communicate or connected 
through another network. aws transitive routin only supported by Transit gateways 
not vpc peering


AWS Direct connect gateways: allows you to connected your on-primises to multiple aws vpc in different region 
can connect to Transit gateways or virtual private gateways 

aws virtual private gateway: is vpn for your vpc which can help you connect to aws Privately but this works for one vpc when you 
have soo many vpc use transit gateway it does the same jobs as aws virtual private gateway
